# Private ERE transport — SOURCE review handoff

## Status and authority

SOURCE/type-only packet, NOT transport or engine acceptance. ROOT explicitly
retains the original phase's publication HOLD: six compiler children retired,
but administrative/transitive process accounting cannot establish compliance
with its64-process grant. This fresh publication does not repair that history.
R01 seven reporting conflicts remain HELD; native12 and all32 transport families/
60 runtime variants remain UNRUN. No Workers, product imports, Shell `=~`, native
or private-engine execution occurred in either type-only cohort or publication.

Source commits: `65f0e080` initial additive transport and `0f36459c` explicit owned
Worker stdout/stderr refusal. Full commit identities are in PUBLICATION.json.
No existing engine, expr/legacy transport, shell/runtime/conditional, public
options/exports, package or shared documentation was edited by these commits.
The provisional five-file engine is b5; only R02 has independent acceptance.

## Complete source scope

All files are under `src/commands/regex-execution/ere/transport/`:

- `protocol.ts`: private request/result/failure schemas and private errors.
- `accounting.ts`: seven engine counters, grant reconciliation, separate T/H.
- `validation.ts`: exact own-data frames/identity/cardinality/span validation.
- `wire-engine.ts`: same-local-ledger compile/match adapter; canonical nonmatch.
- `worker-entry.ts`: static sibling entry, ready frame and serial request guard.
- `owner.ts`: fixed Worker acquisition, output refusal, timeout/retirement owner.
- `root.ts`: lazy invocation-root owner, sessions, shared serialized queue.

Final source/tool/fixture seal SHA256:
`f6ff74e59b15c98e230a2011af8c5c21d6922e44599bc88084a3705846cc55d1`.
SEAL-v2.json binds12 source inputs (five unchanged engine, seven transport),
241 tooling files, exact Node22.22.2 and declaration fixtures. Source selection
is not current HEAD or a coherent whole-package/API integration claim.

## Retained type evidence, not runtime tests

TYPE-01 and TYPE-02 each contain three compiler child receipts: source/declaration
compile0, positive declaration consumer0, negative consumer2 with exactly
TS2353 at2:108, TS2322 at3:59, TS2345 at5:47. Both retain342 captured diagnostic
bytes and24 emitted files (12JavaScript +12declarations). TYPE-02 does not rescore
TYPE-01; the source-only output-ownership correction is REVISION-v2.md.

Publication verifies the retained emitted hashes against each original RESULT,
and the copied source/tool/consumer inputs against each committed seal. It checks
raw output lengths/diagnostics and child IDs/status against retained receipts.
Raw RESULT/OUTER files had no independent historical hash seal; their new hashes
authenticate retained publication bytes, not retroactive tamper-proof history.
There is no compiler retry or artifact regeneration. Work/tool trees remain
owned retained staging; no cleanup, foreign staging or product modifications.

## Runtime proposal — all UNRUN and awaiting a separate ROOT decision

The authoritative VALIDATION.json remains the exact32-family/60-variant DATA
manifest, with its hash and individual family/variant mapping in PUBLICATION.json.
Preserve those identities rather than replacing them with type checks.
Proposed later ceiling:40minutes inclusive cleanup/publication;48OS children,
peak3;24actual Worker starts cumulative;128MiB capture/768MiB work;30s case and
120s build. SOURCE/synthetic protocol/accounting/ownership precedes real Workers.
Source, offline-installed and physically-moved static asset closures require a
new finite dispatch/child/variant map, exact transform/fault controls and grant.
These are proposed ceilings, not executions or a presently ready runtime seal.

The sibling uses no legacy expr pool/reply changes. Original B/F feeds worker
ledgers; grants share cumulative work/state/allocation/capture counters, with
pattern/subject highwater and no refund for unknown sent consumption. Parent
T=A/H=W is ADDITIONAL logical accounting, not a combined byte/RSS cap. Requests
prepay2(47+4n+p+s); reply/result capacity479. Exact metadata/traversal/live-retention
coverage still needs independent SOURCE review and future runtime contrasts.
Queue interpretation is64waiting plus one active, as explicit in DECISIONS-v2.

## Concrete qualifications for the SOURCE reviewer

1. New static entry/engine import graph and Worker flags/output streams have no
   inherited loader or application-Worker admission. Own-stream closure, startup,
   handler-install failures, output refusal and termination joins are UNRUN.
2. Session close marks active work cancelled and joins bounded settlement;
   caller abort is checked around that settlement, not universal immediate
   preemption. Unknown replies/crash/timeout cannot mint engine credit.
3. Validate schema constants, actual metadata counts and all copied/retained
   ownership independently. Types do not prove exact T/H accounting or any RSS
   guarantee. Structured clone occurs before parent frame validation; hostile
   compromised-Worker allocation containment is not claimed.
4. Falsy caller/error/cleanup precedence and singleflight close paths require
   actual fault-injection proof. No BASH_REMATCH writer/publication is present.
5. New internal declarations may later ship through dist. No public package
   exports/options changed; no promise that internal types are unobservable.
6. Capture disambiguation remains the unchanged provisional engine behavior;
   neither transport typechecking nor publication adjudicates R01/native parity.

Publication's observed process events and qualification are in PUBLICATION.json
and its outer/raw logs. No historical process probes or invented descendants.

