# Signed Bash source preparation — no build execution

2026-08-29. ROOT's source/DATA-only grant; acquisition/provenance qualification
does not qualify a native runtime, process fence, or differential oracle.

## Exact authority and capture clarification

- Signature result commit: `fe5d87a215310cbe847bee99bbe3c7650aa3f6e3`.
- This procedure's preseal: `36a6722d9fe5fe1dc257b9dfb3d8691ead8322db`.
- Reauthenticated all 133 committed verification-v2 blobs, then the 33 acquired
  objects, 66 prior authority artifacts, 26 closure identities and controller.
  All sixteen stored pair outcomes and literal machine streams still agree.
- Every signature's signing and explicit primary fingerprint is
  `7C0135FB088AAF6C66C650B9BB5869F064EA74AB`, attributed by the preserved official
  GNU project → Ramey profile → published public-key chain, not signature hints.
  This step reauthenticates the earlier signature evidence, not sixteen new runs.
- Previous terminal-display truncation hid a commit summary. The actual owned
  sixteen stdout/stderr pairs are complete: sizes match the original per-child
  capture counters, content matches committed blobs, and stdout exactly matches
  the preserved machine-status rows. No raw artifact was repaired or shortened.
- Initial zero-child `keyring`/`KEYRING` collision, distinct-path correction,
  previous trailing-space artifact, and every original signature result remain.

## Actual source result

Signed archive SHA256:
`0d5cd86965f869a26cf64f4b71be7b96f90a3ba8b3d74e27e8e9d9d5550f31ba`.
Complete tar inventory: 1,603 members, 36,698,647 regular payload bytes,
37,934,080 decompressed framing bytes. Zero links, special files, AGENTS-named
members, aliases or excluded members. Every header checksum, regular payload
hash, framing/padding, path and directory ancestor was checked before extraction.
Unsupported tar metadata would refuse; this is not a general tar implementation.

Fresh owned source: `/tmp/safe-bash-reference-source-20260829-fn91Rw/bash-5.3`.
Fifteen unchanged, authenticated patch bodies applied serially, all exit 0 with
zero fuzz and literal captured statuses. The old header prefixes resolve only
inside the fresh owned work parent; no signed patch was rewritten. Patchlevel
was checked before/after every patch, ending at the source declaration 15.
No source-version-to-executed-version inference follows.

Final inventory: 1,602 entries excluding the root directory; canonical tuple
SHA256 `75c692f66095ad85848915f50e9357e506ed9664415f48ce6104cafa7269368e`.
`RUN-01/FINAL-SOURCE-INVENTORY.json` defines the UTF-8 traversal ordering and
no-LF JSON serialization. Fifteen distinct changed paths match patch headers;
all other regular files retain archive payload hashes. The full pathname set is
checked, not only old file hashes. Original archive modes are retained as data;
staged files are 0600 and directories 0700, so source scripts are not executable.

Twenty-three native children (8 metadata readers + 15 patch invocations) all
reported close; source controller 21,668.0415 ms, combined native capture 4,811
bytes. No configure, make, compiler, generated helper, Bash or native oracle ran.
`RUN-01/INPUT-POSTCHECK.json` rechecks signed inputs/authority/closure after work.
Fresh final publication separately rechecks staged-source membership and hashes.

The decompressed scratch tar was removed only after its owned handle closed;
the exact patched source tree remains deliberately retained for ROOT's next
decision. No open child or file handle remains. Do not overwrite/reuse this
source as a build directory; any build uses a newly admitted separate root.
No private checkout or product file changed. GNU licensing and COPYING remain
unaltered source data, not a shipped product dependency or copied instructions.

## Tool and closure status

Pinned `/usr/bin/patch` SHA256
`ca8aaa5fa4bd9dfaf4b3be251b18372f25f07483946e7d06b505e5a5fb0a6a84`
has only libSystem in its inspected load commands; existing system-cache/dyld
identities were reauthenticated before/after its use. No external patch helper
or shell command was requested. Trusted CLT llvm-otool read metadata only.

`TOOLS.json` contains 26 finite observations (25 present, `/usr/bin/expr` absent).
CLT clang is now stream-hashed (290,664,032 bytes), not executed, unlike the old
survey's smaller per-file ceiling. Make, compiler, ar/ranlib, linker, shell and
bootstrap utilities have explicit sizes/modes/hashes. Their path names are not
version evidence. SDK link resolves to `MacOSX26.5.sdk`; SDK contents are NOT
admitted yet. Linker requires unresolved `@rpath` libtapi, libcodedirectory,
libLTO and libswiftDemangle; ranlib/libtool also references libLTO. Complete
transitive build-tool/SDK/utility closure is a remaining admission obligation.
No guessed rpath resolution or ambient Homebrew fallback is approved.

`BUILD-RECIPE-DETAILS.json` and `RUN-01/BUILD-SOURCE-OBSERVATIONS.json` bind static
recipe/header findings to source hashes and line indices without copying prose.
Top-level Program is bash; the templates declare CC/CC_FOR_BUILD/AR/RANLIB and
bundled Readline/termcap/localization dependencies. Source references include
mkbuiltins, mkversion, mksignames, mksyntax, config.status and conftest programs.
Reference presence is not a claim that every conditional helper will execute.

## Resource accounting and limitations

The launch ledger reserves 63 process roles through final publication: 13 tool
shells before publication, 23 source-operation native children, the Git tree
reader, controllers and explicit Git/editing commands; final publication adds
its shell/editor/controller/add/commit/log. Missing initial command lookups were
not successful executable starts. No CLI leaves or recursive build jobs ran.
The exact per-call role breakdown is in `PROCESS-LEDGER.json`; this is declared
launch accounting plus observed closes, not independent kernel descendant/RSS
measurement. Peak requested process chain is shell → controller → native child.

The 30-minute / 64-start / peak-3 / 128-MiB capture / 512-MiB work ceilings were
not renewed. Actual source-operation body uses an additional 15-minute maximum
within that grant, not a new allowance. Publication reports source/evidence
logical bytes; transient tar plus staged source remained below 80 MiB, excluding
unchanged external tool files that were streamed rather than copied. No hard
memory, arbitrary-process preemption, race-free hostile-host or fence claim.

Next action: review `BUILD-PROPOSAL.md`, resolve its admission conditions and
request ROOT's separate build GO. Until then, wait; do not execute build recipes.

